From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:41:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: quit a game from the in-game menu or by holding Home

On the iPhone a running game had no way back to the launcher: the
player had to close the app in the app switcher. Two ways now open a
quit prompt over the game, the Mac's (home_quit_mac.h) in look: "Quit
<game>?", a note, and Quit and Cancel pills of one fixed width in every
language.

- The in-game menu (the gear) ends with "Quit <game>", destructive and
  on its own. The gear stays while a controller hides the other touch
  controls, so this works with touch and with a controller.
- Holding a controller's Home button for 2 s opens it too, as on the
  Mac (home_quit.h). The host already claims Home. iOS 27 respects the
  claim when the Home button setting for apps lets the app decide, and
  the log names the setting once.

A tap on Quit or A quits. A tap on Cancel or outside the card, B or a
new press of Home closes it. While it is open the game is told it lost
the focus and gets no input, as on the Mac.

Quitting ends the process. One game runs per process (dm_profile() and the
host's early loading run once), so the engine cannot hand the window back to a launcher. The cloud saves
go out as when the app goes to the background, then the host ends as
on SIGTERM (dm_host_shutdown). iOS cannot start an app again by itself,
so the player opens it again from the Home Screen. DM_HOME_QUIT_TEXT
carries the texts, as on the Mac.

quit_prompt.h is Core Animation and Core Text only, so
tests/quit_prompt checks its layout, hits and touch steps on the Mac in
six languages and can draw it to PNGs (QP_CAPTURE_DIR).

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1115
Reason: Players on the iPhone need a way back to the launcher from a running game: Quit in the in-game menu and the Home hold (#421)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#421
